   ],
   "duration": 6.729,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Same table, two very different questions.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 3.105
    },
    {
     "text": "Watch how differently each one gets answered.",
     "start": 3.525,
     "end": 6.379
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.6,
   "true_peak": -1.9,
   "wpm": 116,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "02": {
   "hash": "d8ff8f22933663f7",
   "takes": [
    "37dce557007cb5f3a27b",
    "8590f9f1d6d48f2db4f6"
   ],
   "duration": 10.165,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "One order, found by its id, through an index that was already sitting there.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 5.3
    },
    {
     "text": "A handful of pages touched, and it is done before you would notice.",
     "start": 5.72,
     "end": 9.815
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.5,
   "true_peak": -1.9,
   "wpm": 159,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "03": {
   "hash": "01b6c59e162722b6",
   "takes": [
    "7b66debac5ac8e0e51ba",
    "1279b480d7143c857a35"
   ],
   "duration": 9.628,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Now ask for a total instead, across every single row.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 4.157
    },
    {
     "text": "The index cannot help with that, so the engine has to walk the entire table.",
     "start": 4.577,
     "end": 9.278
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.4,
   "true_peak": -2.3,
   "wpm": 156,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "04": {
   "hash": "77343e5943a2bede",
   "takes": [
    "f1bca315780299173fe5",
    "c88cf5848951d590b77e"
   ],
   "duration": 10.735,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "That total only actually needs one column out of the six this table has.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 4.775
    },
    {
     "text": "So does the engine get to skip the other five, or does it read them anyway?",
     "start": 5.195,
     "end": 10.385
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.4,
   "true_peak": -1.9,
   "wpm": 168,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "04a": {
   "hash": "29d1ec07493886ba",
   "takes": [
    "aa3729d867d94d28d509",
    "bf13b5d7bce320e33ac5"
   ],
   "duration": 12.166,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "It reads them anyway. A row's columns sit packed together in the same block on disk.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 5.771
    },
    {
     "text": "There is no way to grab just one column's bytes without pulling the whole row along with it.",
     "start": 6.191,
     "end": 11.816
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.3,
   "true_peak": -2.0,
   "wpm": 168,
   "wer": 0.125,
   "exact": false,
   "tolerated": [
    {
     "line": "It reads them anyway. A row's columns sit packed together in the same block on disk.",
     "said": "rows columns",
     "heard": "rose column"
    }
   ]
  },
  "05": {
   "hash": "188799b45813a0c0",
   "takes": [
    "bf4daa7574676a37dfe7",
    "8a65f5db609489aea3db"
   ],
   "duration": 10.969,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Here is exactly how little of each row that one column really is.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 4.801
    },
    {
     "text": "And none of that waste is a bug. It is just what storing by row means.",
     "start": 5.221,
     "end": 10.619
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.6,
   "true_peak": -3.3,
   "wpm": 159,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "06": {
   "hash": "33b6b23829af2b43",
   "takes": [
    "28d5ebdc63f9e068b807",
    "be6288193efe379556f4"
   ],
   "duration": 14.126,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Flip the storage around, column by column instead of row by row, and the waste disappears.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 7.952
    },
    {
     "text": "Needing five columns out of a hundred now means reading roughly five percent of the table.",
     "start": 8.372,
     "end": 13.776
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.5,
   "true_peak": -1.9,
   "wpm": 136,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "07": {
   "hash": "4d73a57c6d2e41c7",
   "takes": [
    "c3df833fb881e513bf9c",
    "3f0449f554d44f2464c3"
   ],
   "duration": 13.936,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Splitting data into small tables is exactly what makes independent transactions cheap and safe.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 6.87
    },
    {
     "text": "That same split is also what forces a big aggregate query to stitch everything back together first.",
     "start": 7.29,
     "end": 13.586
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.4,
   "true_peak": -2.0,
   "wpm": 133,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "08": {
   "hash": "e612603578388f3d",
   "takes": [
    "5de343fc969b5b679fec",
    "0a2e8c4986dd626a5f58"
   ],
   "duration": 13.121,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Few rows, read whole, for point work. Few columns, read whole, for scans.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 5.821
    },
    {
     "text": "Carry that forward, because the next refresher names the relationships underneath both of them.",
     "start": 6.241,
     "end": 12.771
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.6,
   "true_peak": -1.9,
   "wpm": 123,
